---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BriefingForm from '../../components/BriefingForm.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { icon } from '../../data/controls';

// Import your team/logo images from src/assets/
import logoImage from '../../assets/meaning.png';

const standards = [
    'SMB1001 Silver certified, with all Gold controls in place and independent audit pending',
    'At ASD Essential Eight Maturity Level Two across all eight strategies',
    'Built on the same Microsoft security controls we implement for clients',
];


---

<BaseLayout
    title="About Decoheron | Security You Can Prove"
    description="Decoheron is a Melbourne cyber security firm founded by Thomas Ludbrook and Robert Shea. We make the Microsoft security you already own work properly, and prove it."
>

    <div class="dh-page">
        <!-- 1. Hero and Why We Exist -->
        <section class="pg-hero pg-hero--about">
            <div class="pg-wrap">
                <p class="pg-hero__label">Why Decoheron</p>
                <h1 class="ph-hero__title">
                    <span>Decoheron was founded</span><br>
                    <span>on a different belief...</span>
                </h1>
                <div class="pg-hero__lede">
                    <p>...security should be a finished outcome, not an endless process.</p>

                    <p>Cyber threats are evolving faster than most professional services firms can keep up with. While many security providers sell more tools and ongoing services, we focus on delivering measurable security outcomes.</p>
                    <p>Decoheron helps accounting firms, law firms and wealth managers reduce risk using the Microsoft security controls they already own. We implement, validate and continuously attest security controls aligned to Australian standards, providing certainty instead of assumptions.</p>
<p>We don't replace your MSP. We strengthen your environment so they can operate more effectively, while you gain a secure, compliant, and resilient business with evidence to prove it.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- 2. The Founders -->
        <section class="pg-band pg-band--paper">
            <div class="pg-wrap">
                <div class="mb-5">
                    <div class="mb-4">
                        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold text-primary">The founders</h2>
                    </div>
                    <!-- PREPARER NOTE: add founder headshots when available. Until then, keep this two-column layout without image placeholders rather than grey silhouettes. -->
                    <div class="row g-4">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="card h-100 p-4">
                                <div class="mb-3">
                                    <h3 class="h4 fw-bold mb-1 text-primary">Thomas Ludbrook</h3>
                                    <p class="text-secondary mb-0 fw-medium">Founder &amp; Commercial Director</p>
                                </div>
                                <!-- PREPARER NOTE: confirm you're comfortable naming Haylix, Microsoft and Insentra publicly. -->
                                <p class="mb-3 text-body">Thomas has spent 28 years in technology leadership across Australia and Asia Pacific. He started his career as a developer, spent seven years as CEO of cloud managed services provider Haylix, and has held senior roles at Microsoft APAC and Insentra. Running an MSP showed him how often organisations pay for Microsoft security capability they never fully use.</p>
                                <p class="mb-0 text-body">At Decoheron, Thomas leads client relationships and makes sure every engagement is scoped, priced and delivered as a fixed outcome.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="card h-100 p-4">
                                <div class="mb-3">
                                    <h3 class="h4 fw-bold mb-1 text-primary">Robert Shea</h3>
                                    <p class="text-secondary mb-0 fw-medium">Founder &amp; Technical Partner</p>
                                </div>
                                <!-- PREPARER NOTE: Rob's bio keeps to the level of detail already public on the site. Confirm with Rob before adding anything more specific about his background. -->
                                <p class="mb-3 text-body">Robert brings 30 years of security experience across battlefield systems, high-assurance computing and enterprise defence. In those environments, a control is either proven to work or treated as absent. He brings that same discipline to every Decoheron engagement.</p>
                                <p class="mb-0 text-body">Robert designs the controls we implement and the automation we deploy them with. He has a long-standing fascination with information flow, domain theory and quantum physics.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="pg-band pg-band--white ab-aside">
            <div class="pg-wrap">
                <div class="row justify-content-center align-items-center g-4">
                    <div class="col-md-4 col-lg-3">
                        <Image src={logoImage} alt="Decoheron Name and Brand Mark" class="img-fluid mx-auto d-block" style="max-height: 140px; object-fit: contain;" loading="eager" />
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-8 col-lg-7">
                        <p class="fw-bold text-primary small mb-1">Why "Decoheron"?</p>
                        <p class="text-body mb-0">In quantum physics, decoherence is the point where uncertain possibilities settle into a single, observable state. We take uncertain security and make it definite, and evidenced.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>
    <BriefingForm hidden={true} />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
    .pg-hero__lede p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
    .pg-hero__lede p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

    .ab-aside { padding-top: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.5rem); padding-bottom: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.5rem); }

    .ab-principles {
        list-style: none;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        display: grid;
        gap: 2rem 2.5rem;
    }
    @media (min-width: 640px) { .ab-principles { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
    @media (min-width: 1000px) { .ab-principles { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
    .ab-principle { border-top: 2px solid var(--dh-navy); padding-top: 1.1rem; }
    .ab-principle__icon { display: grid; color: var(--dh-indigo); }
    .ab-principle__icon :global(.dh-ico) {
        width: 2rem;
        height: 2rem;
        fill: none;
        stroke: currentColor;
        stroke-width: 1.8;
        stroke-linecap: round;
        stroke-linejoin: round;
    }
    .ab-principle__text { margin: 0.75rem 0 0; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.55; }
    .ab-principle__text strong { display: block; font-family: var(--dh-serif); font-weight: 500; font-size: 1.375rem; line-height: 1.2; color: var(--dh-navy); margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
</style>
